{"segs": ["PA_ja_225:0.4"], "en": "5. The Khantivaṇṇa Jātaka “O King,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_225:1.1", "PA_ja_225:1.2"], "en": "I have a man who is occupied with all my affairs;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_225:1.3"], "en": "“If he has committed even a single offense,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_225:1.4"], "en": "what do you think about that?", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_225:2.1"], "en": "“We too have a man.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_225:2.2"], "en": "“Such a one exists here;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_225:2.3"], "en": "rare is one endowed with all the factors—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_225:2.4"], "en": "patience is what we prefer.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
